  /// reader can pronounce its process dead. Best-effort — a failed
  /// remove leaves the file for the next sweep, and readers only ever
  /// delete inside the `.presence` directory they are listing.
  ///
  /// A file with a [SessionPresence.pid] and a host [pidAlive] probe is
  /// deleted only when the probe reports the process dead (a suspended
  /// process may resume heartbeating — its file stays, whatever its
  /// age). Without a pid or a probe the file's own age decides:
  /// `touchedAt` older than the cleanup grace, or — for torn files
  /// whose timestamps do not parse — the file mtime as the fallback
  /// age. Within the grace the file only drops out of the listing.
